The answer is (C) gas. 

Here's my reasoning:

* "I turn polar bears white" - This could be a reference to the effect of frost or dew on animals, which makes them look white.
* "I make guy have to pee" - Carbonated drinks (like champagne) make people urinate more frequently due to increased fluid intake.
* "I make girls comb their hair" - The bubbles in champagne may make them want to brush their hair, or it could be a play on words for the phrase "comb their hair" being used for champagne.
* "I make celebrities look stupid" - A bubble can make someone look foolish or silly.
* "and normal people look like celebrities" - Bubbles can add a touch of glamour or celebrity-like quality to people, especially children.
* "I turn pancakes brown" - Bubbles can make pancakes look brown due to the Maillard reaction, a chemical reaction that occurs when amino acids and reducing sugars are exposed to heat, leading to the formation of brown products.
* "and make your champagne bubble" - Bubbles are an essential component of champagne.
* "If you squeeze me, I'll pop" - When you squeeze a gas, it releases its pressure and "pops."
* "If you look at me, you'll pop" - Looking at a bubble can make it pop, especially if it's a soap bubble.

Considering the creative and poetic language used in the riddle, the answer (C) gas fits the description best.
